xmodel/ideation-20260829T1517Z-crosspoll-opus5.log:10:**Item 2 — `G5-COLLAPSE` = PASS_WITH_REPAIR.** Rebuilt all 49 rows from `exact_terms` under a fresh name-declared jet-major ring map (49/49 digest, terms, and Singular text). Every load-bearing computation reproduces: the residuals `Phi4`, `Phi3` coefficient-for-coefficient, the four-branch decomposition, the exclusion, the witness. I added a second exact method — the resultant of the two binary quadratics is `-256(s²+64t²)²`, which derives the trichotomy directly and explains Sol's square law.
xmodel/ideation-20260829T1517Z-crosspoll-opus5.log:18:**Item 5 — TD12.** MST-4 is route-general (verified at four states), so the sibling `(17,13,17i)` makes `j=13` automatically an exact derivative — conditional on the unreviewed S typing. That **answers Fable's Card A** rather than running it. Sol's translation-Ward card is self-defeating at its own dependencies. And I refuted my own `TD12-ROW-PROPORTIONALITY`: the td12 cascade has no common typed unknown block, so the test is vacuous.
