xmodel/max12-812-order2-affine-faber-a-delayed-load-h15-arcwise-gate-a-hostile-review-grok-v2-20260826.md:127:Laurent-to-ordinary connection. The first possible negative `z`-principal part of `C^{3/2}` is the grade-30 polar part of `(3/8) Delta^2/Q`. Polynomial summands contribute nothing to `h_j` for `j>=1`. The charged first-block lemma supplies a lower-unitriangular diagonal-one map from `(h1,...,h4)` to the first four ordinary rows, with `Phi_k` independent of `h_j` for `j>k`. A complete initial ordinary block of length four at grade 30 therefore vanishes if and only if `h1=h2=h3=h4=0` at that grade. Moving connection coefficients (functions of `Q=Q0+sigma Q'`) multiply already-vanishing earlier negative `z`-coefficients, of which there are none, or else raise the grade. The connection cannot tie grade 30.
