xmodel/ideation-20260829T0002Z-grok46.md:139:Mechanism: for many complete-split primes `p \notin \{2,3,5,7\}`, specialize the existing D21 affine block plus the four explicit E-branches to `F_p` and test existence of `(sigma, tails)`. This is not CRT, not reconstruction of coordinates, and not Grok C1 (C1 is Nullstellensatz at primes that *already have* points). An empty prime is an obstruction to an S-integral model point of D21+E, hence of any D43 point that specializes to that block. A nonempty prime is weak and expected at the registered frames.
xmodel/ideation-20260829T0002Z-grok46.md:175:**Claim, scoped.** After substituting the four provisional `K0`-rational E-branches into the reviewed D21 band-20 affine block, either some complete-split prime `p \notin \{2,3,5,7\}` has no `F_p`-point, or every tested such prime has a point. The first outcome obstructs an S-integral model point of D21+E. The second is consistent with C1 at the registered frames and does not construct coordinates.
