xmodel/sol-connections.log:5375:xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:3046:SHEET6.md:10:- **1c. RECON correction**: "no independent reproof of ≤5 exists" is WRONG. Sigray's thesis Theorem 9.1 proves td(f,g) ≥ 6 for any counterexample, independently of Żołądek, same year, different machinery (decorated Eggers–Wall trees vs Newton–Puiseux charts). Never journal-published (zbMATH lists only his monodromy + kp′q−lpq′ papers) but cited as the bound by Makar-Limanov (arXiv:2106.06869) and Borisov (arXiv:1901.04073: "current best lower bound ... is 6"). Caveats on BOTH proofs: Żołądek's neighboring gcd sections have a **documented gap** (GGV arXiv:1401.1784: Lemma 4.10 "claims without proof that I₂ ⊂ (1/m)Γ(f₂)"; his claimed B>33 fails, B≥16 stands only via GGV's independent reproof) — his topdeg-5 sections have no reported gap but are unaudited; Sigray's thesis is unrefereed. Also flagged: arXiv:2407.13795 (Moskowicz, 2024, 8pp) claims NO Keller map has prime field-extension degree — unpublished, treat as unvetted; if ever verified it would exclude 7 and make 6, 8, 9 the whole frontier.
xmodel/sol-connections.log:5376:xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:3047:SHEET6.md:14:- **(A) Żołądek's Newton–Puiseux charts** (reconstructed from zbMATH + Nguyen Van Chau arXiv:0804.3172v2 + MIMUW seminar abstract): resolve (f,g) at infinity in BOTH source and target; near each divisor use multivalued charts (x^{−1/m}, ξ) — truncated fractional-power series x(Σc_k x^{−k/m} + ξx^{−n/m}) where ξ replaces the Puiseux tail ("left and right Newton-Puiseux charts", Chau). The Keller map becomes near-monomial in charts; jac≡1 forces rigid exponent+leading-coefficient relations. Topological degree = sheets over infinity = Σ local degrees over dicritical divisors, with Orevkov's identity Σ(ramification excess at infinity) = td − 1. Case analysis = finite enumeration of dicritical/chart configurations for td ≤ 5; each killed by exponent arithmetic or analytic contradiction.
xmodel/sol-connections.log:5390:xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:3223:notes.md:279:- SHEET6 campaign (4835b13, UNREVIEWED): engine reproduces pilot; Lambda<=7 = 14 rows; td=6 rows 2,3 EXCLUDED; ~15 case-III s-tails + IV-terminals gated on H3 (root-kill). HEADLINE CLAIMS: 3 new thesis errata (E2-E4, lam=0 self-loop families the thesis says don't exist), G2 (St 9.12's kill set can't close its own IV-terminals — unstated H3 load-bearing), G3 (thesis silent on rows 1,5,7,10 => Sigray td>=6 INCOMPLETE AS PRINTED; td<=5 safe via Orevkov/Domrina/Zoladek). If review confirms: sheet-6 exclusion is genuinely open => our campaign = novel work, and RECON's "independent reproof" language needs qualification.
