xmodel/pi1s4-close-residual-hostile-review-sol56-20260831.log:2823:59:**Affine recast, sourced from Neumann–Norbury (arXiv math/0110286, Thm. 2.1), quoting Nori 3.27.** Let `Σ ⊂ C²` be nodal. Let `X` be a blow-up of `P²` resolving the singularities of `Σ` *at infinity*, with `D = X − C²`. If the proper transform of each component satisfies `C̄_i · C̄_i > 2 r(Σ_i)` and meets `D` transversally, then `π₁(C² − Σ)` is abelian (because `X − D = C²` is simply connected, so `N` is the whole group). This is Nori 3.27 with `E` the divisor at infinity, not a new theorem.
