xmodel/max12-812-order24-coefficient-infinity-review-grok-v2-20260825.md:196:A competing interpretation — derivatives of the Rees polynomials `Phi_ell` at `Lambda=0` — does not disturb V2. In `(5.3)` the loads enter only as `Lambda^{12-j}k_j`, so `\partial Phi_ell/\partial k_j` vanishes on `Lambda=0` by the prefactor, independently of whether `[K^{j/4}]_-` vanishes. That is a statement about the compactified chart, not about the unscaled tail map that the erratum differentiates while holding `f` fixed. It does not resurrect the false identity `(7.2)`, and it does not restore transversality of `Phi` in the `B_i` directions, which still vanish by `(7.1)`.
