    88	section. Nothing in that argument uses `G=0`: the shear moves `C1 -> C1+lambda E1`
    89	and `C2 -> C2 + lambda b Z eta^2` and leaves the pair's cell and pole data
    90	unchanged. Hence **`c5 = 0` may be assumed on the live section too**, and
    91	
    92	```text
    93	C2 = d Z eta s.
    94	```
    95	
    96	Every statement below is made under `c5 = 0`; the shear that achieves it is a
    97	polynomial automorphism of the target, so emptiness statements transport back.
    98	
    99	**`E0` as an identity.** `E0` reads `2(q r' - p' s) = kappa`. Wherever the
   100	combination `4Z(q r' - p' s)` occurs (it occurs in `E1eq`) it may be replaced by
   101	`2 kappa Z`. So
   102	
   103	```text
   104	E1eq:  6 D1 r' - 4q'E1 + 2q E1' + 4C1 s' - 2C1' s + 2 kappa Z = 0.        (1.1)
   105	```
   106	
   107	**Two operators.** For `Y in C[Z]` set
   108	
   109	```text
   110	M(Y)  = 2Z eta Y' -   eta Y - 4Z eta' Y,
   111	M2(Y) = 2Z eta Y' -   eta Y - 2Z eta' Y.
   112	```
   113	
   114	If `Y != 0` has degree `k`, then `deg M(Y) = e+k` with leader
   115	`eta_e Y_k (2k-1-4e)` and `deg M2(Y) = e+k` with leader `eta_e Y_k(2k-1-2e)`.

