   688	## Lane report contract amendment: seal-at-completion (2026-08-31 17:35Z)
   689	
   690	Two lanes returned sealed skeletons on 2026-08-31 (a provider ended its
   691	turn after writing the skeleton; a 128K-output-cap kill mid-response),
   692	because the previous template had lanes write the `<!-- BODY-END -->`
   693	seal into the initial skeleton — making `report_state=BODY_SEALED`
   694	unable to distinguish a finished report from a crashed one.
   695	
   696	Binding contract for every future lane prompt:
   697	
   698	1. The skeleton written as the lane's first action MUST NOT contain the
   699	   `<!-- BODY-END -->` marker.
   700	2. Sections are appended as separate bounded writes (target under
   701	   ~1,500 words per write; never the whole report in one response).
   702	3. The standalone `<!-- BODY-END -->` line is appended only after the
   703	   final section is on disk, with nothing after it.
   704	4. If the budget runs short: finish the current section, type every
   705	   remaining section OPEN in one short paragraph each, then seal.
   706	
   707	Under this contract, `PARTIAL_NO_MARKER` correctly identifies crashed
   708	or under-delivered lanes, and the divert machinery banks their partial
   709	content. Coordinator-side: a `BODY_SEALED` receipt no longer implies
   710	substance; harvest still requires reading the report. Queued ops debt

